<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest>

  <!--
    Offline downloads intentionally add NO manifest configuration from this library. Client apps
    must add them manually if using offline downloads, because they can be sensitive permissions

    Mux Player's offline download support relies on a foreground Service (MuxDownloadService) and a
    PlatformScheduler JobService, which in turn require sensitive permissions:
      - android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE
      - android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_DATA_SYNC
      - android.permission.RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED

    We deliberately do NOT declare the Service, the JobService, or these permissions here. Merging
    them from the library would force them onto every app that depends on mux-player, even ones that
    never download anything - and sensitive permissions like these affect Play Store review and user
    trust. They should only be enabled by apps that actually use offline downloads.

    If you use offline downloads, declare the Service, the PlatformScheduler JobService, and the
    permissions in your OWN app's AndroidManifest.xml. The `app` and `automatedtests` modules in
    this repo have a working, copy-pasteable example. This will be documented in the dev guide.
  -->

</manifest>